Standard edition/


*.json
# The canonical rollout exclusion data is source, not generated data. It must
# be tracked so the exporter, scrubber, reset and publish paths cannot drift.
!tools/rollout/exclusions.json
# The rollback records are the evidence of what a public reset replaced: the
# old and new tag shas, the old and new release ids, the old..new range. They
# are written by the reset orchestrator and must survive in the history.
!docs/reset-*-rollback.json
decrypted/
# Exactly three key files are TRACKED: the container IKM, the comment IKM and
# the Ed25519 manifest signing key - they are what lets this repository build
# its own .AvroEnco containers with no second repository to fetch from.
#
# 'keys/*' rather than 'keys/' so the directory itself stays reachable and the
# negations below can name their files. Everything else under keys\ - most
# importantly the keys\old\<timestamp>\ copies that rotate_ikm.ps1 writes to
# preserve a superseded IKM - remains local and untracked.
#
# A NEW key file must be added to the negation list below, or it is silently
# untracked: it would build on this machine and fail to build from a clone.
keys/*
!keys/avroenco.key
!keys/avrocomments.key
!keys/manifest_ed25519.key
*.enc

# The *.json guard above exists to keep PLAINTEXT mapping sources
# (assets\Ansi V*.json and friends) out of the repository. Two JSON artifacts
# are the opposite: they must be committed, because they are what makes a
# build reproducible and verifiable.
#
#   resources.lock.json          - Ed25519-signed pins (sha256 + size) for every
#                                  shipped container. Committed: this is the
#                                  offline gate, and it contains no plaintext.
#   .../AvroShieldSelfTest/fixtures/*.json
#                                - signed sample lock/manifest used by the KAT
#                                  gates. Committed: the gates must run offline
#                                  on a clean clone with no keys present.
!resources.lock.json
!AvroEncoEngine/tools/AvroShieldSelfTest/fixtures/*.json

# The '*.res' guard above is for compiled leftovers. Three .res files are the
# opposite: they are real inputs, force-added long before this file was tidied.
#   Layout\Internal_Layout.res, Skin\Internal_Skin.res - the built-in skin and
#   layout, linked by their loader units.
#   Layout\AvroBaseline.res - the embedded ANSI baseline, linked by
#   uAvroBaseline.pas. Its source is AvroBaseline.rc, which needs the plaintext
#   container to rebuild - so a build must NOT have to run brcc32 to link it,
#   or a fresh clone (which deliberately has no plaintext) would fail.
!Keyboard and Spell checker/Layout/AvroBaseline.res

# Maintainer-only plaintext sources, restored by
# tools/resource-sync/fetch_sources.ps1 for a build and never committed.
assets/*.json
# Exception: the ANSI version mapping tables (Ansi V1.json .. Ansi V100.json)
# are committed, so any ANSI version stays reproducible from a clean clone.
!assets/Ansi V*.json

# The encrypted ANSI mapping containers are BUILD ARTIFACTS: they are produced
# by AvroEncoEngine\tools\AvroEncoBuilder\build_avroenco.bat and published
# through the resource repository, not through this one (the public export
# withholds them in tools\rollout\exclusions.json). They carry no key material
# - the static-leak gate proves that - but committing them would ship the
# whole shipped mapping set, and the authored sources beside them are the
# record that is meant to stay private.
assets/*.AvroEnco

# The same mappings keyed for the Qt converter instead of the root IKM (see
# tools\secrets\derive_converter_key.py). Same rule as above: build artifacts
# written by build_avroenco.bat from assets\Ansi V*.json, withheld from the
# public export, never committed.
assets/converter/*.AvroEnco

# The public provider is tracked. The production provider is installed over it
# by tools\secrets\fetch_secrets.ps1 and marked skip-worktree so it cannot be
# committed by accident.

# Windows Explorer folder artefact: it is written into assets/icons whenever the
# shell rewrites a file name there (the layout icons are regenerated at
# runtime), it is read by nothing in the code and nothing in the build.
desktop.ini

# Local config / data
*.ini
*.log

# Ai agent
.freebuff
.kilo

# Release artifacts produced by tools/release/build-installers.ps1
Output/

# Qt converter build output (Converter\MakeDist.bat; see Converter\.gitignore)
Converter/build/
Converter/dist/
Converter/CMakeCache.txt
Converter/CMakeFiles/
Converter/*.exe
Converter/*.obj

# Delphi keyboard build output (rebuilt by tools\release\build-installers.ps1
# on every pass; build\ is cleaned before each build)
/build/
# Release assets land here (installers and portable zips with the REAL
# root-secret unit compiled in). They must never be committed: the export
# withholds paths, not content, so a committed Output\ would ride the next
# public push. tools\release\build-installers.ps1 writes it every release.
/Output/
# Python bytecode from tools\resource-sync\*.py and tools\secrets\*.py. They are
# run directly, and an import between them drops __pycache__ into a tracked
# folder - which then reads as a dirty working tree to the rotation script.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The public update manifests. The '*.xml' guard above would ignore them, but
# updates\versioninfo.xml and updates\versioninfo_beta.xml ARE the update feed
# the application reads from Avro-Keyboard main - they must be committed.
# release\gen_manifest.ps1 writes them, and nothing else may live in updates\.
!updates/
!updates/*.xml
